---
source: crates/vps-ready/src/modules/firewall_inbound/tests.rs
expression: FirewallInbound.notes(&facts)
---
- "always accepts TCP 22, the current SSH ports (this session's, sshd's listeners and `Port`), whatever `allow` says"
- "Docker is installed: input from docker0 and br-* is accepted, so containers can reach services on the host; a compromised container can reach all of them, as with no firewall"
- "Docker publishes tcp/5432: that traffic is forwarded to containers and does not pass this firewall (FW-002); publish on 127.0.0.1 or filter it in DOCKER-USER"
- "other chains also filter incoming traffic, and a packet must pass each of them: ip filter INPUT"
- "`ufw status` does not show these rules; `nft list table inet vps_ready` does"
- "nftables.service is enabled: restarting it flushes the whole ruleset and removes this table until `systemctl restart vps-ready-firewall.service`"
- "if this installs nftables, rollback leaves it installed"
